  "details": "Many games for decades have used a few different methods for allowing countless sounds to play simultaneously without heavy performance hit or dealing with sounds cutting out.   For example if in a world where something plays too many sounds (such as a game world that instantiates audio sources on a collision) completely prevents avatar audio from playing.\n\nThey tend to either pre-mix everything into a single multi-channel output source, and/or they use systems that filter out sounds by their distance, volume, specified priority, etc, to cull overflow audio sources by those that are least important and/or least audible.\n\nAudio is extremely important to immersive experience in vr, and not just in worlds, but avatars as well, and it's been given the short end of the stick for far too long.",
